      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        150.28863525390625,
        527.4443969726562,
        164.8416290283203
      ],
      "text": "Source case:  Person with TB disease who infected others in a new setting. This could be the index",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        163.59864807128906,
        297.9967956542969,
        178.04164123535156
      ],
      "text": "patient or another person who was not identified.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        185.1925048828125,
        527.4390258789062,
        199.74549865722656
      ],
      "text": "Systematic screening for tuberculosis disease:  Systematic identification of people at risk for TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        198.5025177001953,
        527.390380859375,
        212.9455108642578
      ],
      "text": "disease in a predetermined target group by assessing symptoms and using tests, examinations or",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        211.70252990722656,
        527.41552734375,
        226.14552307128906
      ],
      "text": "other procedures that can be applied rapidly. For those who screen positive, the diagnosis needs",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        224.9025421142578,
        527.428955078125,
        239.3455352783203
      ],
      "text": "to be established by one or several diagnostic tests and additional clinical assessments. This term is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        238.10243225097656,
        527.4212036132812,
        252.54542541503906
      ],
      "text": "sometimes used interchangeably with “active tuberculosis case-finding”. It should be distinguished",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        251.3024444580078,
        454.85955810546875,
        265.7454528808594
      ],
      "text": "from testing for TB infection (with a TB skin test or interferon-gamma release assay).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        272.89630126953125,
        527.4110107421875,
        287.4493103027344
      ],
      "text": "Treatment outcomes and relapse:  Categories for treatment outcomes used in this document and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        286.2064208984375,
        527.3309936523438,
        300.6494445800781
      ],
      "text": "the term “relapse” were applied according to the definitions agreed for use by TB programmes, unless",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.974169731140137,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        299.40643310546875,
        175.79147338867188,
        313.8494567871094
      ],
      "text": "otherwise specified. 12,13",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.0003356933594,
        527.4341430664062,
        335.5533447265625
      ],
      "text": "Tuberculin skin test (TST):  Intradermal injection of a combination of mycobacterial antigens that",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        334.310302734375,
        527.4354858398438,
        348.7533264160156
      ],
      "text": "elicit an immune response (delayed-type hypersensitivity), represented by induration, which can be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        347.51031494140625,
        352.7232971191406,
        361.9533386230469
      ],
      "text": "measured in millimetres. TST is used to diagnose TB infection.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        366.42022705078125,
        527.4033813476562,
        383.6572265625
      ],
      "text": "Mycobacterium tuberculosis Tuberculosis (TB):  Disease state due to  . In this document, it is commonly",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.973769187927246,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        382.4142150878906,
        355.2102966308594,
        396.85723876953125
      ],
      "text": "referred to as “TB disease” to distinguish it from “TB infection”.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.32421875,
        527.42333984375,
        418.56121826171875
      ],
      "text": "Mycobacterium  Tuberculosis infection:  State of persistent immune response to stimulation by",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        414.52423095703125,
        527.2291870117188,
        431.76123046875
      ],
      "text": "tuberculosis  antigens with no evidence of clinically manifest TB disease. This is referred to as “TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        427.7242431640625,
        527.4325561523438,
        444.96124267578125
      ],
      "text": "M.  infection” as distinct from “TB disease”. There is no gold standard test for direct identification of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        440.9241943359375,
        527.4290771484375,
        458.1612243652344
      ],
      "text": "tuberculosis  infection in humans. Most infected people have no signs or symptoms of TB but are at",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        456.918212890625,
        502.77032470703125,
        471.3612365722656
      ],
      "text": "risk for TB disease. The term “latent TB infection” has been replaced by the term “TB infection”.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        478.5121154785156,
        527.39013671875,
        493.06512451171875
      ],
      "text": "Tuberculosis preventive treatment (TPT):  Treatment offered to people considered at risk of TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        491.8221130371094,
        524.407470703125,
        506.26513671875
      ],
      "text": "disease to reduce that risk. Also referred to as “treatment of TB infection” or “TB preventive therapy”.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        513.4161376953125,
        527.5489501953125,
        527.9691162109375
      ],
      "text": "Underweight:  Among adolescents, this usually refers to a body mass index below 18.5. Among",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
